          "comment": "In good form in recent weeks and and won't mind if the ground turns soft here",
          "spotlight": "Went close at Uttoxeter (2m5f, good to soft) last month and his recent Perth third (2m4f, good) was also a good effort; won't mind if the ground turns soft here and has a fighting chance if he takes to this unique track at the first attempt; swaps visor for refitted blinkers; tongue-tie removed.",
          "quotes": [],
          "stable_tour": [
            {
              "quote": "He did very well last season as he was a big baby and just struggled physically. He was a bit disappointing at Aintree on Sunday, but it was his first time in a handicap and he'll improve for the run. He's a 3m-plus chaser, who handles softer ground, and we'll go over fences now. 01-11-23"
            },
            {
              "quote": "He's a nice youngster who won his point-to-point at Curraghmore by 30 lengths in the spring before joining us. He made his rules debut at Kelso last month over 2m6f when a close third. He stayed on the whole way up the straight and will be worth following , as he gains more experience. He ran last week at Haydock but never managed to get in a blow and the ground probably played a big part. There's plenty to come from him. 07-12-22"
            }
          ],
