          "comment": "11yo who has not won since 2019 and is probably watched on return for new yard",
          "spotlight": "11yo who is without a win since the 2019 Ascot Stakes at the Royal meeting; extended his good record at that meeting last term but his form was very mixed in 2025; now returns for new yard after 255 days off and is hard to know what to expect; regular headgear is missing.",
          "quotes": [
            {
              "date": "2019-06-18",
              "horse": "The Grand Visir",
              "horse_id": "hrs_6345598",
              "race": "Ascot Stakes (A Handicap)",
              "race_id": "rac_9510254",
              "course": "Ascot",
              "course_id": "crs_52",
              "distance_f": "20",
              "distance_y": "4390",
              "quote": "The Grand Visir ran well at Newmarket and fortunately he dropped the 1lb that allowed him in to this race. We weren't sure he'd stay the trip but Richard gave him a lovely, patient ride. Turning for home I thought there were only two travelling well, him and Time To Study. Time To Study probably hasn't stayed and he stayed all the way to the line. It's great to have a Royal Ascot winner - Ian Williams, trainer."
            },
            {
              "date": "2018-05-26",
              "horse": "The Grand Visir",
              "horse_id": "hrs_6345598",
              "race": "Amix Ready Mixed Concrete Handicap",
              "race_id": "rac_9108866",
              "course": "Haydock",
              "course_id": "crs_598",
              "distance_f": "16",
              "distance_y": "3565",
              "quote": "We have been riding The Grand Visir wrong. We had been riding him handy over shorter trips as he's one-paced but there is a long straight here and we dropped him in and rode him patiently and he proved he stayed well. He's in the Ascot Stakes and the Northumberland Plate and he'd get into that sort of race now - William Haggas, trainer."
            }
          ],
