          "comment": "4-20; won at Ludlow in March but not at best since and 10lb claimer takes over",
          "spotlight": "Good ground suits and she notched win number four from 20 attempts at Ludlow (2m5f) in March; not at best since, though, finishing well behind Mostly Sunny at Uttoxeter last time; 10lb claimer takes over.",
          "quotes": [],
          "stable_tour": [
            {
              "quote": "She scoped with mucus after running at Stratford last week, but Adam Wedge said she gave him a nice feel and he couldn't believe she stopped. She was treated for ataxia after the race, but I imagine that's because she was full of mucus and couldn't get any oxygen in. 02-11-22"
            },
            {
              "quote": "She's a good-ground mare who's back in cantering after having a holiday. She's as hard as nails but not overly big and is much better running in a better race with less weight. I'm not sure she genuinely stays 3m and her ideal trip is probably a good gallop over 2m6f. She's a good jumper and I wouldn't rule out going back over fences. 29-01-25"
            }
          ],
