          "comment": "Has won three of his last four starts but getting dangerously high in the weights",
          "spotlight": "Has won three of his last four starts, most recently edging out Vintage Fizz over C&D a month ago (good; effective on soft); 4lb higher now and he is getting dangerously high in the weights.",
          "quotes": [
            {
              "date": "2025-06-20",
              "horse": "The Flier Begley",
              "horse_id": "hrs_18332706",
              "race": "Associated British Ports 'Summer Plate Trial' Handicap Chase (GBB Race)",
              "race_id": "rac_11653278",
              "course": "Market Rasen",
              "course_id": "crs_910",
              "distance_f": "21.5",
              "distance_y": "4709",
              "quote": "The Flier Begley dug deep when I needed him to and thankfully he's a stayer. I was worried the rise in the handicap might catch him out, but he proved me wrong. He's been a revelation since last year. We've won some nice pots along the way and I think Gary [Hanmer, trainer] has found the key to him now, keeping him fresh and well. Some of these older horses enjoy being in a smaller yard. I think he'll have a good chance in that [Summer Plate on July 19], but it depends what the handicapper does. I said to the owners if I win today it will have to be by the smallest of margins! - Jack Hogan, jockey, speaking to Racing TV."
            },
            {
              "date": "2025-04-19",
              "horse": "The Flier Begley",
              "horse_id": "hrs_18332706",
              "race": "Unibet Middle Distance Veterans' Handicap Chase (Series Final)",
              "race_id": "rac_11577553",
              "course": "Haydock",
              "course_id": "crs_598",
              "distance_f": "20",
              "distance_y": "4383",
              "quote": "That was super. We were a little bit disappointed with The Flier Begley's last run and I think we might have gone to the well once too often so we backed off and freshened him up - Gavin Hanmer, trainer."
            },
            {
              "date": "2025-01-17",
              "horse": "The Flier Begley",
              "horse_id": "hrs_18332706",
              "race": "Unibet Middle Distance Chase Series Veterans' Handicap Chase (Unibet  Vets' Chase Series)",
              "race_id": "rac_11496121",
              "course": "Market Rasen",
              "course_id": "crs_910",
              "distance_f": "21.5",
              "distance_y": "4709",
              "quote": "The Flier Begley is a dream to ride, he travels and jumps like a buck. He won quite well in the end. He ran well last time at Haydock and before that he just didn't get home as he was too keen. He's in form now and seems to be showing it. I thought we were up against it with some of the horses here, but we were coming into it with a horse in form. He likes top of the ground and he stays well - Jack Hogan, jockey."
            }
          ],
