          "comment": "Last year's winner seeking a return to form in first-time cheekpieces; dangerous mark",
          "spotlight": "Returning from a similar break when winning this 12 months ago off 1lb higher but was on a four-timer then and is now seeking a return to form in first-time cheekpieces; feasible winner should the new experiment work as the forecast rain won't be an issue.",
          "quotes": [
            {
              "date": "2024-07-20",
              "horse": "Sure Touch",
              "horse_id": "hrs_23537801",
              "race": "Unibet Summer Plate Handicap Chase (Premier Handicap) (GBB Race)",
              "race_id": "rac_11324027",
              "course": "Market Rasen",
              "course_id": "crs_910",
              "distance_f": "21.5",
              "distance_y": "4709",
              "quote": "Sure Touch is a remarkable little horse. I absolutely couldn't have imagined this at all. He was running around in novice hurdles two summers ago and has just progressed, progressed and progressed. I was always very confident to be honest, considering he went off at 14-1. He jumped magnificently - Olly Murphy, trainer."
            },
            {
              "date": "2022-07-16",
              "horse": "Sure Touch",
              "horse_id": "hrs_23537801",
              "race": "Unibet Partnering Great Racing Welfare Cycle Novices' Hurdle (GBB Race)",
              "race_id": "rac_10591958",
              "course": "Market Rasen",
              "course_id": "crs_910",
              "distance_f": "20.5",
              "distance_y": "4539",
              "quote": "I probably didn't do a great job with Sure Touch, not winning through the winter, but he hit the crossbar a few times. We did his wind and obviously the calibre of racing this time of year isn't as strong. Newton Abbot probably did his confidence good. He won well again today and he might be capable of winning under a double penalty. He'll jump a fence next year - Olly Murphy, trainer."
            }
          ],
          "stable_tour": [
            {
              "quote": "He's been ultra-progressive and will go for the Grand Sefton, in which he could run very well if the ground is not too soft. He's a fantastic jumper so we're looking forward to seeing him over the fences. 24-10-24"
            },
            {
              "quote": "He has done us proud this season, winning four times already, and it would have been five but for a head defeat last time at Catterick. He's up to 122 and I think we might squeeze one more out with that rating. He'll go novice chasing in late summer. 22-12-22"
            }
          ],
