          "horse_id": "hrs_35729862",
          "horse": "Ancient Wisdom",
          "dob": "2021-04-12",
          "age": "4",
          "sex": "gelding",
          "sex_code": "G",
          "colour": "b",
          "region": "FR",
          "breeder": "Ecurie Des Monceaux Et Al",
          "dam": "Golden Valentine",
          "dam_id": "dam_6313531",
          "dam_region": "FR",
          "sire": "Dubawi",
          "sire_id": "sir_4127830",
          "sire_region": "IRE",
          "damsire": "Dalakhani",
          "damsire_id": "dsi_3974124",
          "damsire_region": "IRE",
          "trainer": "Charlie Appleby",
          "trainer_id": "trn_255042",
          "trainer_location": "Newmarket, Suffolk",
          "trainer_14_days": {
            "runs": "30",
            "wins": "9",
            "percent": "30"
          },
          "owner": "Godolphin",
          "owner_id": "own_199380",
          "prev_trainers": [],
          "prev_owners": [],
          "comment": "Smart performer on his day and any recent rain would seemingly be a help; gelded now",
          "spotlight": "Still a smart performer on his day and any recent rain would seemingly be a help; close, front-running second in Group 3 at Sandown in April was over 1m2f, after last season's best efforts were at 1m4f and 1m5f; way below that form on his other two starts this year, albeit in Group 1 Coronation Cup on latest; gelded since and big shout if he's on his game.",
          "quotes": [
            {
              "date": "2024-07-11",
              "horse": "Ancient Wisdom",
              "horse_id": "hrs_35729862",
              "race": "Bahrain Trophy Stakes (Group 3)",
              "race_id": "rac_11316292",
              "course": "Newmarket (July)",
              "course_id": "crs_4524",
              "distance_f": "13",
              "distance_y": "2860",
              "quote": "We were quietly confident as Ancient Wisdom was the class horse in the race and was racing on ground that we know he relishes. The plan from here is to head to the Voltigeur if the ground is right and plan our way to the St Leger. He is an autumn horse and we won't jeopardise that by running him on unsuitable ground - Charlie Appleby, trainer."
            },
            {
              "date": "2024-05-16",
              "horse": "Ancient Wisdom",
              "horse_id": "hrs_35729862",
              "race": "Al Basti Equiworld Dubai Dante Stakes (Group 2)",
              "race_id": "rac_11224863",
              "course": "York",
              "course_id": "crs_2782",
              "distance_f": "10.5",
              "distance_y": "2256",
              "quote": "We're happy and most importantly, Will [Buick, jockey] said Ancient Wisdom handled the ground. We were confident we'd handle it, but when you bring extreme conditions he excels in it. Trip-wise he's crying out to step up in trip and he'll come forward for this - he's having a good heave for one of ours. We'll let it all settle down as it's only two and a bit weeks and see how much he progresses from this. He'll come forward a good bit and a mile and a half is definitely his trip. A galloping track [at the Curragh] will be his. We feel a more sterner test suits, whereas Epsom you can be a mile and a quarter horse and win, because you have to be able to travel. This horse will come on a lot and allowed himself more time in the spring than Arabian Crown did - he's still coming in his coat - Charlie Appleby, trainer."
            },
            {
              "date": "2023-10-28",
              "horse": "Ancient Wisdom",
              "horse_id": "hrs_35729862",
              "race": "Kameko Futurity Trophy Stakes (Group 1) (No Geldings)",
              "race_id": "rac_11022024",
              "course": "Doncaster",
              "course_id": "crs_390",
              "distance_f": "8",
              "distance_y": "1760",
              "quote": "That was worth the wait. You don't want anything like that to happen but Aidan's horse looked like he got up okay, that's the main thing. We couldn't be more delighted. We thought Aidan's other horse was going to go forward and when he wasn't there Will (Buick) did his own thing. We know Ancient Wisdom stays and the plan was always to be handy. Charlie always had this race slightly in the back of his mind but he wanted to see how the horse was, and he's been pleasing him and we know he handles soft ground so we gave it a shot. He's very exciting. I think he'll be a horse who's going to want a trip next year. We've obviously got a very good one to beat in the Guineas so we'll see how he progresses over the winter and see how we go - Alex Merriam, assistant trainer."
            },
            {
              "date": "2023-10-14",
              "horse": "Ancient Wisdom",
              "horse_id": "hrs_35729862",
              "race": "Emirates Autumn Stakes (Group 3)",
              "race_id": "rac_11043864",
              "course": "Newmarket",
              "course_id": "crs_988",
              "distance_f": "8",
              "distance_y": "1760",
              "quote": "We were disappointed that we were beat at Ascot, but that race worked out so well you couldn't really be disappointed. I've probably mismanaged Ancient Wisdom running him back at Newmarket. Next year, I do feel a mile and a quarter will be within his compass and I think he will appreciate going a mile and a half. He is a Dubawi and as we know with those middle-distance type Dubawi's you can't force them too much in the spring of their three year old career so therefore something like a Dante might be a target for him. Whether we take a run before the Dante we will just see where we are in the spring, but we have a long winter ahead of us now. It is nice to be able to put these horses to bed on the back of an impressive victory - Charlie Appleby, trainer."
            },
            {
              "date": "2023-06-24",
              "horse": "Ancient Wisdom",
              "horse_id": "hrs_35729862",
              "race": "Join Racing TV Now British EBF Novice Stakes (GBB Race)",
              "race_id": "rac_10946052",
              "course": "Newmarket (July)",
              "course_id": "crs_4524",
              "distance_f": "7",
              "distance_y": "1540",
              "quote": "They went no pace so I thought I'd teach Ancient Wisdom something and he finished off well - James Doyle, jockey."
            },
            {
              "date": "2023-06-09",
              "horse": "Ancient Wisdom",
              "horse_id": "hrs_35729862",
              "race": "GPW Recruitment Carl Foster Memorial EBF Novice Stakes (GBB Race)",
              "race_id": "rac_10929646",
              "course": "Haydock",
              "course_id": "crs_598",
              "distance_f": "7",
              "distance_y": "1532",
              "quote": "We were expecting Ancient Wisdom to run a very good race and he's done that and a bit more. He went to sleep a little round the turn but once we straightened up I asked him to show a bit of interest and he jumped into the bridle and showed a good kick, hitting the line good. I'd say it was everything you would look for in a debut of a potentially smart horse - James Doyle, jockey, speaking on Racing TV."
            }
          ],
