          "prev_owners": [],
          "comment": "Usually front-runner; 1m4f was seemingly too much last time; has a shout if back to form",
          "spotlight": "Usually front-runner these days; three handicap wins last year before he narrowly took a Listed race at Newmarket in November, all about 1m2f on soft or good to soft; fair fourth at Chester on return, before 1m4f on soft was seemingly too much for him on latest start; has a shout if back to form.",
          "quotes": [
            {
              "date": "2024-10-12",
              "horse": "Bolster",
              "horse_id": "hrs_32278484",
              "race": "Coral \"Daily Rewards Shaker\" Handicap",
              "race_id": "rac_11397997",
              "course": "York",
              "course_id": "crs_2782",
              "distance_f": "10.5",
              "distance_y": "2256",
              "quote": "The ground is key with Bolster. He's probably pounds ahead of himself on soft, even heavy ground. It makes such a difference. He stays so well. When he runs on good ground the speed horses just have that extra gear, but from three out today he was away and there was no stopping him. We'll speak to connections but it'll be likely one more or no more runs for him this year - James Cowley, trainer's assistant."
            },
            {
              "date": "2024-05-31",
              "horse": "Bolster",
              "horse_id": "hrs_32278484",
              "race": "Betfred Nifty 50 Handicap",
              "race_id": "rac_11269856",
              "course": "Epsom",
              "course_id": "crs_442",
              "distance_f": "10",
              "distance_y": "2217",
              "quote": "I'd say Bolster is a Group 3 horse - that's where we'll go, but he wouldn't want fast ground. We'll have a good look at an autumn campaign for him - Karl Burke, trainer."
            }
          ],
