          "prev_owners": [],
          "comment": "Lightly raced 6yo who's 2-2 on turf (good to soft); major player if returning to his best",
          "spotlight": "6yo who has had only seven races; most have been on AW but he's won his only two turf starts, on good to soft, including by a head in 1m2f Group 3 at Sandown in April 2024; free-going sort, which may have contributed to his lesser show when front-running favourite at Kempton three months ago; he'd have a major say if returning to his best.",
          "quotes": [
            {
              "date": "2024-04-26",
              "horse": "Okeechobee",
              "horse_id": "hrs_29972635",
              "race": "bet365 Gordon Richards Stakes (Group 3)",
              "race_id": "rac_11237070",
              "course": "Sandown",
              "course_id": "crs_1404",
              "distance_f": "10",
              "distance_y": "2189",
              "quote": "We're very happy with that as it was the first time Okeechobee has really had to get his head down and race. He doesn't have many miles on the clock and we could look at supplementing him into the Prix d'Ispahan at Longchamp next month as we think the race will suit him - Barry Mahon, racing manager to Juddmonte."
            },
            {
              "date": "2024-04-01",
              "horse": "Okeechobee",
              "horse_id": "hrs_29972635",
              "race": "Virgin Bet Every Saturday Money Back Magnolia Stakes (Listed Race)",
              "race_id": "rac_11211005",
              "course": "Kempton (AW)",
              "course_id": "crs_28054",
              "distance_f": "10",
              "distance_y": "2199",
              "quote": "Okeechobee ran great off a 550-day layoff and it was good to see. We couldn't ask for much more off level weights with the winner. We'll look at something like the Gordon Richards Stakes at Sandown - Harry Charlton, trainer."
            },
            {
              "date": "2022-09-29",
              "horse": "Okeechobee",
              "horse_id": "hrs_29972635",
              "race": "Radcliffe & Co Handicap",
              "race_id": "rac_10667826",
              "course": "Salisbury",
              "course_id": "crs_1352",
              "distance_f": "10",
              "distance_y": "2181",
              "quote": "Okeechobee would have been the kind of horse who probably would have won the Cambridgeshire - a strongly run nine furlongs. That's out of the window and he only came into training as a three-year-old, while he'd never done a piece of work on the grass until about a month ago. What he did before that was on pure ability. He's going to progress and has a great temperament. We might run him again and I think there are a mile and ten-furlong Listed races coming up. At the same time, he doesn't want bottomless ground. Ryan Moore said after Kempton he was a Group horse - Harry Charlton, trainer."
            }
          ],
