          "comment": "Reliable and progressive on AW; turf record is a worry, pulled up in the Gold Cup latest",
          "spotlight": "Has raced only four times on turf, with a soft-ground win on first occasion but lesser shows since, already dropping out when he was hampered in the Gold Cup at Royal Ascot one month ago (50-1; pulled up); reliable and progressive on AW, surging to new heights with his two handicap wins this March/April, but he's now 8lb higher than for latest win.",
          "quotes": [],
          "stable_tour": [
            {
              "quote": "He is a nice individual who has had two runs, the most recent at Kempton in February when second over a mile, which is definitely his minimum trip. I will possibly go and try to win over a mile and then head down the handicapping route. I could see him progressing to being an effective 1m4f handicapper in time. I know he has not won yet so you may find it an odd comparison but at this stage of his career, but if I have a horse in the yard that is similar to Deauville Legend then it is him. At this time last year the ‘Deauville' was second on the all-weather, just as was ‘Wonder' was at Kempton last time. And we know that ‘Deauville' progressed all through the year and this one could be the same. Their physicality is also similar in that they are both big, strong colts and I would love to see him win a big handicap somewhere and then the world could be his oyster. 29-03-23"
            }
          ],
