          "comment": "Solid campaign last term (third in this race) and he made a satisfactory return this April",
          "spotlight": "Has run well both starts at Newbury, third off this mark in this race last year; that was a solid campaign and he made a satisfactory reappearance this April, so he should be a strong candidate.",
          "quotes": [
            {
              "date": "2024-05-16",
              "horse": "Kyle Of Lochalsh",
              "horse_id": "hrs_32401796",
              "race": "Al Basti Equiworld Dubai \"City Bowl\" Handicap",
              "race_id": "rac_11253931",
              "course": "Salisbury",
              "course_id": "crs_1352",
              "distance_f": "14",
              "distance_y": "3124",
              "quote": "Hughie [Morrison, trainer] was a bit worried about the ground but Kyle Of Lochalsh managed to get the job done nicely. Considering he handles this ground it could open up some options for him. I think he could climb through the ranks - Billy Loughnane, jockey, speaking on Racing TV."
            }
          ],
          "stable_tour": [
            {
              "quote": "He did really well last year. He won only once but was placed many times, including at Royal Ascot in the Ascot Stakes and in a Listed race in France after that. However, as a result of that, he's now rated 97 and is difficult to place, so you're looking for specifics - he definitely needs soft ground. We need to try to find the right race for him but it won't be easy as we seem to have lost a Listed race or two from the calendar. There's one at the beginning of July at Sandown on Eclipse weekend and that might be the sort of race for him if the ground is right. He could go for the Ascot Stakes again and he might get an entry in the Queen Alexandra on the basis that it might rain at the end of the week, but I don't know whether he'll stay virtually 2m6f. 29-05-25"
            }
          ],
