          "comment": "Not at his best in the Wokingham and now tried in headgear; still has time on his side",
          "spotlight": "Progressive last summer, winning two 6f handicaps at Ascot and ending the campaign with a fine second in a Group 3 over the same C&D; promising return at Salisbury and was well backed ahead of his Wokingham bid four weeks ago, only to drop away in the closing stages; versatile groundwise; still early days and new blinkers could give him a lift.",
          "quotes": [
            {
              "date": "2024-08-10",
              "horse": "Jarraaf",
              "horse_id": "hrs_37407356",
              "race": "Dubai Duty Free Shergar Cup Sprint (Handicap)",
              "race_id": "rac_11338873",
              "course": "Ascot",
              "course_id": "crs_52",
              "distance_f": "6",
              "distance_y": "1320",
              "quote": "We've always liked Jarraaf and his work has suggested that he's pretty smart. Maybe I didn't do the best job with him early on in trying to stretch him over seven. The stiff six at Ascot suits him well and he was at his best in the final furlong. We'll see what the handicapper does and we'll go from there. He's a gorgeous, big horse and hopefully we'll have him next year as well  - Owen Burrows, trainer."
            }
          ],
          "stable_tour": [
            {
              "quote": "He's won twice over six furlongs at Ascot so the Wokingham looks a logical next step. He was a beaten favourite on his return at Salisbury, but he needed the run and was beaten only a length, so I wasn't too disappointed. The ground was also a bit too quick and if it were similar conditions then we'd consider switching to the Buckingham Palace over seven furlongs, although he'd have top weight in that and as it stands I'm keen on the Wokingham. 10-06-25"
            }
          ],
