              "course_id": "crs_338",
              "distance_f": "11.5",
              "distance_y": "2495",
              "quote": "Caspi Star is a big girl and that probably impacts her not being the most fleet of foot out of the stalls, and as a result she was on the back foot from the word go. She was probably finding the track a bit tight all the way and got hampered turning into the straight just as she was coming with her run, but then finished better than anything. There are only positives to take out of it. She'll have learned plenty for this. She's not in the Oaks and we'll have to see what Nurlan [Bizakov] thinks but if she doesn't go there, I'm sure she'll go to the Ribblesdale - Charlie Johnston, trainer."
