          "comment": "Completed double when winning at Goodwood last month and soft ground excuses latest run",
          "spotlight": "Won in Jersey in May and followed up at Goodwood (1m, good) last month; soft ground excuses his below-par run at Carlisle a fortnight ago and he could bounce back with a bold show here.",
          "quotes": [
            {
              "date": "2022-08-28",
              "horse": "Tempus",
              "horse_id": "hrs_15687917",
              "race": "Barriere Prix Quincey (Group 3) (4yo+) (Straight Course) (Turf)",
              "race_id": "rac_10663289",
              "course": "Deauville",
              "course_id": "crs_5356",
              "distance_f": "8",
              "distance_y": "1760",
              "quote": "It's hard to tell how good Tempus is, he's won two Group 3s now so the obvious step now is up to Group 2 level. He would probably get a bit further with the way he settles now, but he's very effective at this trip. I think Archie has some ambitious plans for him - Hollie Doyle, rider."
            },
            {
              "date": "2022-08-11",
              "horse": "Tempus",
              "horse_id": "hrs_15687917",
              "race": "Tattersalls Sovereign Stakes (Group 3) (Colts & Geldings)",
              "race_id": "rac_10619596",
              "course": "Salisbury",
              "course_id": "crs_1352",
              "distance_f": "8",
              "distance_y": "1760",
              "quote": "Tempus is going from strength to strength, we made the entry for the QEII because it's perfectly feasible he'd run well and I'd say he's highly likely to represent us at Ascot - Simon Turner, director of racing for Hambleton Racing."
            },
            {
              "date": "2020-09-04",
              "horse": "Tempus",
              "horse_id": "hrs_15687917",
              "race": "Beefeater Handicap",
              "race_id": "rac_9937941",
              "course": "Ascot",
              "course_id": "crs_52",
              "distance_f": "8",
              "distance_y": "1760",
              "quote": "They've been going slow all day, but it suits Tempus because he relaxes and he's got a turf of foot - he picks up when asked and it would have taken a good one to go past him. He did it well and the next question is can we stay a little further and win the Cambridgeshire? We'll have a roll at that under a small penalty and hope the ground's a bit softer - Harry Charlton, assistant trainer"
            },
            {
              "date": "2020-08-15",
              "horse": "Tempus",
              "horse_id": "hrs_15687917",
              "race": "Unibet You're On Handicap",
              "race_id": "rac_9920274",
              "course": "Newbury",
              "course_id": "crs_936",
              "distance_f": "8",
              "distance_y": "1760",
              "quote": "I think three out Tempus was in trouble, two out he hit a flat spot and took a blow and then his talent got him going again. Normally, when you're tired and get a knock like that it stops you, but he was charging at the line. He needs a flat track and a bit of cut and I wouldn't be surprised if he was running in stakes races next. He's out of Passage Of Time and Prince Khalid will want black type. If it was easy to go to France that's the type of place we'd go - Harry Charlton, assistant trainer."
            },
            {
              "date": "2019-06-12",
              "horse": "Tempus",
              "horse_id": "hrs_15687917",
              "race": "Watch Racing TV Now Novice Stakes (Plus 10 Race)",
              "race_id": "rac_9495330",
              "course": "Haydock",
              "course_id": "crs_598",
              "distance_f": "8",
              "distance_y": "1797",
              "quote": "Tempus bowled along in front comfortably and has done well to make all in that ground. He was probably just a class above his rivals and he should come on again for the run - Jason Watson, rider."
            }
          ],
