              "course_id": "crs_52",
              "distance_f": "8",
              "distance_y": "1753",
              "quote": "Dashing Roger jumped well and I was in a lovely position. I got a little bit of cover, saved ground up there on the inside and we've got a lot of room up there in the home straight. As soon as I pulled him out, he quickened nicely and put the race to bed in a matter of strides. His turn of foot took me by surprise and for a horse to quicken like that in that ground was brilliant. He's a tough animal that loves to run. He is very enthusiastic ? what a genuine, tough little horse - Cieren Fallon, jockey."
