          "prev_trainers": [],
          "prev_owners": [],
          "comment": "Ground likely too quick on reappearance and potential class act giving weight away",
          "spotlight": "Looked potentially smart when smooth winner on 1m4f Ascot handicap debut (soft) last September in first-time cheekpieces; hasn't progressed as might have been expected in three subsequent runs (favourite each time) but not disgraced either and may have found good to firm ground too lively (raced on softer than good otherwise) when fifth of 12 in a York Dante meeting handicap on reappearance (no headgear); still has time on his side and a potential class act giving weight away to lesser opposition in refitted cheekpieces.",
          "quotes": [
            {
              "date": "2024-09-07",
              "horse": "The Reverend",
              "horse_id": "hrs_37658887",
              "race": "Chapel Down Handicap (Heritage Handicap)",
              "race_id": "rac_11361311",
              "course": "Ascot",
              "course_id": "crs_52",
              "distance_f": "12",
              "distance_y": "2631",
              "quote": "That was pretty easy, wasn't it? I'd say The Reverend is pretty good. He over-travelled to the two-furlong pole and I only had to ask him to quicken to get to the leaders and then he extended well. He's a smart performer and there's still more to come. William wanted to put the cheekpieces on to show the true ability he has and he just seemed to be finding his way. With age he'll be even better - David Probert, jockey, speaking to Sky Sports Racing."
            },
            {
              "date": "2023-11-03",
              "horse": "The Reverend",
              "horse_id": "hrs_37658887",
              "race": "Betfred \"Double Delight\" British EBF Novice Stakes (Colts & Geldings) (Div II)",
              "race_id": "rac_11098334",
              "course": "Newmarket",
              "course_id": "crs_988",
              "distance_f": "7",
              "distance_y": "1540",
              "quote": "The Reverend handled the ground better than some of the others but I wouldn't say he relished it; it's pretty disgusting out there. He looked well and behaved well, which was important and what I was pleased to see. It's taken some time to get him here, which you wouldn't necessarily think looking at him, but he's changed a lot over the year and has matured a lot physically and mentally - Maureen Haggas, trainer's wife and assistant."
            }
          ],
