          "comment": "Hard to win with but capable at this level and sharper for last month's return; yard run 2",
          "spotlight": "Hold-up sprinter who isn't easy to win with; capable at this level though and he should be sharper with last month's return to action behind him; stable also run Eldeyaar.",
          "quotes": [
            {
              "date": "2024-11-21",
              "horse": "Rogue De Vega",
              "horse_id": "hrs_34991040",
              "race": "Know Your Limits With BetUK Handicap",
              "race_id": "rac_11444589",
              "course": "Wolverhampton (AW)",
              "course_id": "crs_13338",
              "distance_f": "5",
              "distance_y": "1121",
              "quote": "We were drawn badly so Anthony [Brittain, trainer] said to just tuck Rogue De Vega in and ride for a bit of luck. He's a little bit of a tricky horse but he enjoyed that, coming with one smooth run - Mark Winn, jockey, speaking to Sky Sports Racing."
            }
          ],
          "stable_tour": [
            {
              "quote": "Another who never ran until April, but this son of Lope De Vega has already shown he has a bright future. We tried to buy him as a yearling but could not afford him, but we did eventually purchase him at the Goresbridge breeze-ups. After a debut second place he returned to Chelmsford for his second run and won nicely over 5f. For his last run we went to Bath where he met an in-form horse of George Boughey's yet still ran an encouraging race (second). We will be ready to go any time now and there is a glut of races he could run in so I will speak to Tony before deciding, but I believe he can step up again as he has with each of his three starts. 06-07-23"
            }
          ],
