          "comment": "Oaks winner, form franked by runner-up Whirl, looks a cut above these rivals",
          "spotlight": "By Frankel out of a half-sister to Kingman, cost 1,850,000euros as a yearling; failed to get to grips with the front-running Wemightakedlongway on debut at Cork last October, made amends with a victory over Subsonic at Leopardstown; won Cheshire Oaks on reappearance and took the rise in class in her stride when holding off stablemate Whirl in the Oaks, form franked in the Pretty Polly; still building towards maturity and looks a cut above these rivals.",
          "quotes": [
            {
              "date": "2025-06-06",
              "horse": "Minnie Hauk",
              "horse_id": "hrs_43667281",
              "race": "Betfred Oaks (Group 1) (Fillies)",
              "race_id": "rac_11575707",
              "course": "Epsom",
              "course_id": "crs_442",
              "distance_f": "12",
              "distance_y": "2646",
              "quote": "I'm delighted with Minnie Hauk. She's very classy and Ryan gave her a beautiful ride. He loved her the last day [at Chester] and then again today, so she's very exciting. She's obviously learning - she went to Chester and learnt a lot and was still green, and she was always improving from mid-race. What you love about her is that she's a great traveller; she has a lot of class. Ryan felt he was going very easily today on her and usually what that means is that she will be able to step up a couple of grades into even higher-class races. It's lovely for the lads and for everyone to have another filly like that. - Aidan O'Brien, trainer.Minnie Hauk is still learning a little bit. Aidan had a lot of faith in her. She travelled around strongly and I got to her quite easy, and then she was a little green in front. When the other filly came back she went on again. She's a talented filly and she stayed on well. I'm very happy with her and hopefully she'll build on this - Ryan Moore, jockey."
            },
            {
              "date": "2025-05-07",
              "horse": "Minnie Hauk",
              "horse_id": "hrs_43667281",
              "race": "Weatherbys ePassport Cheshire Oaks (Listed Race) (Fillies)",
              "race_id": "rac_11604333",
              "course": "Chester",
              "course_id": "crs_338",
              "distance_f": "11.5",
              "distance_y": "2495",
              "quote": "That [the Oaks] is the plan. Aidan always thought Minnie Hauk would improve a lot for this run. She's a very kind, uncomplicated filly with a great attitude. The step up in trip obviously helped and you'd be thinking of the Oaks. Ryan was niggling away just to get her interested, but she's kind and always answers to the jockey and she just kept on finding. Ryan was quite sweet on her - Paul Smith, representative of Coolmore, owners."
            }
          ],
          "stable_tour": [
            {
              "quote": "She's improved a lot and done really well physically. She ran twice last season, finishing second at Cork and winning well at Leopardstown. She's a mile-and-a-half filly and is one for an Oaks trial. 07-04-25"
            }
          ],
