          "comment": "Late developer, 2-2 last season, off the track over a year, Al Riffa yard's main hope",
          "spotlight": "Lightly raced late developer won both starts last season, a minor four-runner race at Killarney (1m6f, soft) and an emphatic 5l success in the Queen Alexandra Stakes at Royal Ascot over an extended 2m5f (gd-fm); off the track since and this a big ask on his return; stable has a better chance with Al Riffa.",
          "quotes": [
            {
              "date": "2024-06-22",
              "horse": "Uxmal",
              "horse_id": "hrs_27068790",
              "race": "Queen Alexandra Stakes (Conditions Race)",
              "race_id": "rac_11299561",
              "course": "Ascot",
              "course_id": "crs_52",
              "distance_f": "21.5",
              "distance_y": "4763",
              "quote": "Uxmal was very good. We had a nice prep run the last day in Killarney and he did it really well. He was always going to handle the ground and the step up in trip was never going to be a worry and Joseph had him spot on for the day. It's great to reward him like this. I know it's the last race and he's been hitting the crossbar but I would like to thank him and the owners for giving me this opportunity. This lad is really relaxed and when I hit the front I could really hear the noise. I just kept my head down and made sure I we got the job done - Dylan Browne McMonagle, jockey."
            }
          ],
          "stable_tour": [
            {
              "quote": "He was an impressive winner of the Queen Alexandra last year but picked up a little niggle in the race so didn't run again. We'll work our way back to the same race this year. He undoubtedly has plenty of stamina and it's a race that suits him. 24-04-25"
            }
          ],
